feat: Leen Coffee monorepo — schema, customer app, and five app scaffolds

Sets up the Leen Coffee marketplace as a pnpm + Turborepo workspace on the
same shape as aljahis: six apps and five shared packages over one Supabase
database.

Database (supabase/, live on nwedptckqbcktdqgoixr)
  Roasteries, coffees, carts, orders, subscriptions, loyalty, riders and
  reviews. Money is integer halalas throughout. RLS on every table, with
  auth.uid() wrapped as (select auth.uid()) and role checks behind SECURITY
  DEFINER helpers in a `private` schema that PostgREST does not expose.

  `orders` has no INSERT policy at all: the only way to create one is
  place_order, which prices the cart from the product rows, applies VAT and
  promo, splits the basket into one sub-order per roastery, captures
  commission, decrements stock under a deterministic row lock, awards loyalty
  points and empties the cart — all in one transaction. The client says what
  it wants, never what it costs.

  Guard triggers cover what policies cannot: a merchant cannot list itself on
  the storefront or set its own commission, a rider cannot approve itself, and
  nobody can promote their own profile to admin.

Customer app (apps/customer-mobile)
  All fifteen screens from the Claude design, wired to the live database:
  onboarding, phone + OTP auth, home, explore, roastery, product, cart,
  checkout, confirmation, live tracking, subscriptions, rewards, profile and
  addresses. Arabic-first with real RTL mirroring, Arabic-Indic digits via
  Intl, and diacritic-folding search implemented on both sides of the wire.

Scaffolds
  merchant-mobile (live order board), delivery-mobile (job board with
  race-safe claiming), and three Next.js apps — storefront, merchant order
  desk, admin console — each signed in and reading real data.

Verification
  pnpm build and pnpm typecheck are green across all sixteen tasks; 12 unit
  tests in @leen/lib; scripts/e2e-order.mjs runs nineteen checks against the
  live database as a real signed-in customer, including that a direct INSERT
  into orders is refused and that promo codes are not enumerable.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
